      "side": 1,
      "message": "APP uid is based on userId and appId.\nSo it\u0027s better to follow actual uid ranges.\nYou can see [UserHandle](https://source.corp.google.com/h/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/base/core/java/android/os/UserHandle.java;l\u003d374-380;drc\u003d98b10195430aba7226e57b7d3b7cb0784842ae08) and [ConnectivityServiceTest](https://source.corp.google.com/h/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Connectivity/tests/unit/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityServiceTest.java;l\u003d544-551;drc\u003d0d06b9460a76e66ce69f8ea3ec309a4a688f8559)\n\nI think you can do something like the following\n```\nprivate const val PRIMARY_USER \u003d 0\nprivate const val SECONDARY_USER \u003d 10\nprivate val PRIMARY_USER_HANDLE \u003d UserHandle(..)\nprivate val SECONDARY_USER_HANDLE \u003d UserHandle(..)\n\n// sms app names\nprivate const val SMS_APP1 \u003d \"...\"\nprivate const val SMS_APP2 \u003d \"...\"\n\n// sms app ids\nprivate const val SMS_APP_ID1 \u003d 100;\nprivate const val SMS_APP_ID2 \u003d 101;\n\n// UID for app1 and app2 on primary user\n// These app could become default sms app for user1\nprivate const val PRIMARY_USER_SMS_APP_UID1 \u003d UserHandle.getUid(PRIMARY_USER, SMS_APP_ID1)\nprivate const val PRIMARY_USER_SMS_APP_UID2 \u003d UserHandle.getUid(PRIMARY_USER, SMS_APP_ID2)\n\n// UID for app1 and app2 on secondary user\n// These app could become default sms app for user2\nprivate const val SECONDARY_USER_SMS_APP_UID1 \u003d UserHandle.getUid(SECONDARY_USER, SMS_APP_ID1)\nprivate const val SECONDARY_USER_SMS_APP_UID2 \u003d UserHandle.getUid(SECONDARY_USER, SMS_APP_ID2)\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 61,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 64,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "e9dd5ed906afe547b650e73541ea04d031052dba",
